      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TORN (3) finds a nice race. He doesn't win out of turn but is going well for this on his preferred heavy ground, fourth in a tougher race at Seymour two back before just missing at Wangaratta. Sets a solid benchmark and will take holding out. BLOW ON THE DICE (4) has been racing well without winning. Last start finished second, beaten 3.5 lengths, over 1400m at this track. Heading the right way off past couple and should be right there. NEVRA QUEEN (7) has been freshened up since she finished seventh over 2000m at Bordertown seven weeks ago. Back sharply in trip but form prior around this sort of trip was solid and she can figure. EIRE TO THE JUNGLE (2) raced on the pace over 1400m at Casterton last time and went on to win by one length, his second victory to date. No reason he can't measure up again. SAVETHEBESTTILLAST (6) backs up quickly but probably doesn't want it too wet.",
